// kyoten::input — devices into a game's actions (the first slice's step 8, KYR-54; design/input.md § Decided). The
// binder reads the bindings records and the samples a platform hands in, and makes each owed step's hand-off: every
// player's action values, split by each sample's time.
//
// - **Bindings are content,** keyed by action, then device (question 2): a control's name, a list of them, or an object
//   of an action kind's parts, by `@kama/window`'s names (`"ArrowUp"`, `"RightShoulder"`, `"LeftX"`), each read by the
//   package's own reader, so a misspelling is refused at load with every name listed. The mouse's motion is kyoten's
//   own: `"Motion"` for a `Vector2`, `"MotionX"` and `"MotionY"` for one axis.
// - **A `Digital` entry's gestures** (the fourth part, design/input.md § Decided, 2026-11-24) recognize a pattern over
//   time in the order written, each reading the on and off of the one before it, the first the entry's controls:
//   `hold`, `tap`, `longTap`, `multiTap`, `repeat` (a press again while held), `toggle`, `delay`, `chord` and
//   `sequence`. They run in real time, on the samples' clock: a deadline (a hold's time passing) lands in the step whose
//   end passes it, and each step's hand-off carries each digital's `progress`, how far the gesture under way has come.
//   A gesture naming no time takes the `input` record's. `interruptible` comes with the fourth part's later commit.
// - **A chord's modifiers and a sequence's steps** (question 2) are controls of the entry's scheme, the keyboard and the
//   mouse together or the pad, with kyoten's `Shift`, `Control`, `Alt` and `Meta` for either side, or digital actions,
//   held as their own bindings hold them; actions holding each other in a circle are refused, and each action is
//   settled after every action it holds. A chord turns on only when its control presses while every modifier is
//   already held, and lets go when either does; a sequence's steps come in order, each within its time of the one
//   before (a step out of order passed over, the first step again starting it again), and its control last.
// - **A chord masks** (question 3): a press of its control while its modifiers are held, or the last press of a
//   sequence whose steps all came, goes to that entry alone; every other entry reading the control, a value's part
//   included, sees none of it until it lets go. A chord's own modifiers keep their bindings. `"masks": false` lets both
//   see it.
// - **A value action's entry takes a `chord` alone,** which gates it: its value counts only while every modifier is
//   held, the mouse's motion only what moved while they were.
// - **An entry's filters** (the third part, design/input.md § Decided, 2026-11-23) reshape the value its parts make, in
//   the order written, before a delta's seconds, on a step's hand-off and on Output's newest alike: `deadZone`, `scale`,
//   `invert`, `curve`, `clamp`, `remap`, `normalize`, `digital` and `smooth`, whose state each path keeps apart. On the
//   mouse's motion, a distance moved, only `scale`, `invert` and `smooth`, since the rest would change with the step's
//   length; `smooth` smooths its speed. A value out of its filter's range is refused at load, naming the action.
// - **Split by time** (question 1): a step takes the samples that arrived by its end and were not handed off yet, so a
//   frame that owes no step keeps its input for the next.
// - **Player 1** has the keyboard and the mouse throughout, and **the first pad pressed**, locked until it disconnects
//   (question 4): while one is locked another pad does nothing. A pad takes the lock with a button pressed, never a
//   stick or a trigger's travel alone, so a drifting or knocked stick cannot take player 1.
// - **One action on several controls** (`["ArrowUp", "KeyW"]`) is held while any of them is, and its edges are those
//   of that combined state.
// - **A stick's directions are controls** (the third part's question 2): `LeftStickUp`, `LeftStickDown`, `LeftStickLeft`,
//   `LeftStickRight` and the right stick's, kyoten's own names, each its axis's half toward it, 0 to 1, after the
//   stick's default dead zone, wherever a control is read.
// - **A value made a button presses at one point and lets go at a lower one:** a stick's direction bound to a `Digital`
//   at the `input` record's `stickThreshold` (0.5 and 0.375), and any pad control of a `Digital` entry with its own
//   `threshold` (`{ "control": "RightTrigger", "filters": [ { "threshold": 0.6 } ] }`, a bare number letting go at three
//   quarters of it), read from its travel or its axis through its default dead zone. A pad button bound with no
//   threshold keeps `@kama/window`'s events, so a press and its release between two readings are both kept.
// - **Edges, per step** (kyoten::frame::Digital): a press and its release inside one step show the press, held, on that
//   step and the release on the next; a release and a press inside one step show both, held.
// - **A control is on at `Gamepad::PressedAt` of its travel or more,** `@kama/window`'s own threshold, for every device.
// - **The default dead zones** (the third part's question 1): the `input` record's, every layer's laid over, given to
//   every stick an entry reads and every trigger's travel unless the entry's own filters name a `deadZone`: radial,
//   before its own filters, where the entry reads both axes of one stick as its x and y, and on each axis or trigger
//   alone otherwise. A record naming none reads raw.
// - **Player 1's active scheme** (the second part's question 1) is the kind of device that last drove them: a key or a
//   mouse button pressed or the mouse moved is `KeyboardMouse`; the locked pad's button pressed, a trigger past
//   `PressedAt` or a stick past half its travel is `Gamepad`, so drift cannot switch it; the locked pad gone, back to
//   `KeyboardMouse`. Each step's hand-off carries it as of the step's end.
// - **A value action** (`Analog`, `Vector2`, `Vector3`; the second part's questions 1 and 2):
//   - an entry's parts make its value: an `Analog`'s `positive` less its `negative`; a `Vector2`'s `right` less `left`
//     and `up` less `down`, or its `x` and `y`; a `Vector3`'s with `backward` less `forward` (forward is -Z) or `z`.
//     Up is positive on every device: a stick's Y and the mouse's motion down the window are turned over. Keys make a
//     direction no longer than 1, so a diagonal is not faster (Unity's DigitalNormalized, Godot's `get_vector`);
//   - a part on several controls reads the most actuated, and **a state** (any value whose record says no `delta`) the
//     most actuated of its devices' entries, as of the step's end (Unity's default, Godot's strongest);
//   - **a delta** sums them: the mouse's motion that landed in the step, and each control held times the step's
//     seconds, so a stick turns as far each second whatever the rate. The mouse's motion bound to a state is refused.
// - **Output's newest** (`newest`, frame-phases § Decided: "presentation reads, such as camera look, take the newest
//   sample each frame"): every sample taken so far applied, each state as of the newest, each delta since Output's last
//   frame at the frame's seconds, whether or not a step took them. In a frame that owes no step the samples are applied
//   early, which loses nothing: each still lands in the next step's hand-off, since a step's edges and motion are cleared
//   after it is handed off, and every sample taken arrived before the next step's end.
//
// It is tier `Module`, outside the simulation's fence, as the module that reads devices must be, and names
// `kyoten::frame` and `kyoten::records` alone of the engine; the generated `run` builds it and hands it to the loop.

import { std::collections::DynamicArray, std::collections::SortedMap, std::memory::Owned, std::math::Vec2,
         std::math::Vec3, std::math::sqrt, std::serialization::text::json::deserializeJsonBuffer,
         kyoten::frame::Digital, kyoten::frame::Handoff, kyoten::frame::Sample, kyoten::frame::SampleKind,
         kyoten::frame::Device, kyoten::frame::InputSource, kyoten::frame::ActionList, kyoten::frame::Time,
         kyoten::frame::Scheme,
         kyoten::records::BindingRecord, kyoten::records::ControlEntry, kyoten::records::ActionKind,
         kyoten::records::FilterRecord, kyoten::records::FilterKind, kyoten::records::InputRecord, std::math::exp,
         std::math::pow, std::math::floor, kyoten::records::GestureRecord, kyoten::records::GestureKind,
         kyoten::records::GestureTimes, kyoten::records::GestureName,
         window::Key, window::PadButton, window::PadAxis, window::PointerButton, window::Gamepad };

export { Binder, BindingError };

comptime int32 NO_PAD = -1;
// How far a stick goes before it says the pad is in use: half its travel, so a drifting or knocked stick does not.
comptime float32 STICK_IN_USE = 0.5;
// A gesture with no deadline: int64's most, past every step's end.
comptime int64 NOT_DUE = 9223372036854775807;
comptime float64 NS_PER_SECOND = 1000000000.0;

// What a gesture hands the next: its input on, off, or pressed again while on (a `repeat`'s).
type enum Change { On, Off, Again }

// One device's entry of a digital action: its controls, `controls[from]` up to `controls[to]`, on while any is; its
// gestures, `gestures[gestureFrom]` up to `gestureTo`; and what the last of them makes, which is what the action sees.
type value DigitalEntry {
    public int32 action;
    public isize from = 0;
    public isize to = 0;
    public isize gestureFrom = 0;
    public isize gestureTo = 0;
    public bool raw = false;
    public bool on = false;

    public ctor make(int32 action) { this.action = action; }
}

// One gesture as the binder runs it: its kind, its entry, its times in nanoseconds and its count, as the record's
// `GestureRecord` says (`a`, `b`, `count`, `on`); and what it has seen: its input, what it makes, when its input last
// went on, its next deadline, the presses it has counted (a `multiTap`'s) or made (a `repeat`'s), and the time of the
// last change it holds back (a `delay`'s).
type value Gesture {
    public GestureKind kind;
    public isize entry;
    public int64 a = 0;
    public int64 b = 0;
    public int32 count = 0;
    public bool enabled = true;
    public bool input = false;
    public bool out = false;
    public int64 since = 0;
    public int64 due = NOT_DUE;
    public int32 taps = 0;
    public int64 queuedTo = 0;
    // A chord's modifiers or a sequence's steps, `modifiers[modFrom]` up to `modTo`; whether it masks; and the time of the
    // last press a sequence took, which no step may take again.
    public isize modFrom = 0;
    public isize modTo = 0;
    public bool masks = true;
    public int64 tookAt = -1;

    public ctor make(GestureKind kind, isize entry) {
        this.kind = kind;
        this.entry = entry;
    }
}

// One thing a chord holds, or one step of a sequence: a group of controls, `controls[from]` up to `controls[to]`, any of
// which counts (kyoten's `Shift` is both shift keys), or a digital action, where `action` is 0 or more; the gesture it
// is of, or -1 for a value entry's chord, which gates the value; its step in a sequence; and whether it was on when last
// looked at, so a change is seen once.
type value Modifier {
    public isize gesture;
    public isize from = 0;
    public isize to = 0;
    public int32 action = -1;
    public int32 step = 0;
    public bool was = false;

    public ctor make(isize gesture) { this.gesture = gesture; }
}

// A change a `delay` holds back until `at`; `done` once handed on.
type value Pending {
    public isize gesture;
    public int64 at;
    public Change change;
    public bool done = false;

    public ctor make(isize gesture, int64 at, Change change) {
        this.gesture = gesture;
        this.at = at;
        this.change = change;
    }
}

// Why bindings were refused at load: one line each, every refusal at once.
type resource BindingError implements Error {
    DynamicArray<string> linesField = DynamicArray.empty();

    public ctor make() { }

    public fn void add(string line) { this.linesField.add(item: give line); }
    public const fn bool any() { return this.linesField.length() > 0; }
    public const fn const ref DynamicArray<string> lines() { return this.linesField; }
    public const fn string message() {
        string all = "";
        foreach (const ref string l in this.linesField.iterConst()) { all = all.isEmpty() ? copy l : all + "; " + l; }
        return all;
    }
}

// One control a digital action is bound to, and whether it is on: a key, a mouse button or a pad button by its edges
// (`Control`), or a value made a button, a pad button's travel or a stick's half (`Travel`, `Axis`), which presses at
// `press` and lets go at `release`, read through its default dead zone.
type value Bound {
    public Device device;
    public int32 control;
    public bool on = false;
    public SampleKind kind = SampleKind::Control;
    public bool flip = false;
    public float32 half = 0.0;
    public Zone zone = Zone::None;
    public float32 press = 1.0;
    public float32 release = 1.0;
    // A press a chord or a sequence took for itself, which this control does not see until it lets go.
    public bool hidden = false;

    public ctor make(Device device, int32 control) {
        this.device = device;
        this.control = control;
    }
}

// How a value entry's parts make its value.
type enum Shape { One, Pair, Keys2, Axes2, Keys3, Axes3 }

// Which default dead zone a source reads through on its own.
type enum Zone { None, Stick, Trigger }

// One control a value is read from: a key's or a button's edge (1 or 0), a pad button's travel, a stick's axis, or the
// mouse's motion; and what it reads now.
type value Source {
    public Device device;
    public SampleKind kind;
    public int32 control;
    // A Y read up positive: a stick's LeftY or RightY, the mouse's motion down the window.
    public bool flip;
    // A stick's direction: its axis's half toward it, 1 the positive half, -1 the negative, 0 the whole axis.
    public float32 half = 0.0;
    // As of the last sample taken: a state.
    public float32 value = 0.0;
    // The default dead zone it reads through, per axis: none, a stick's or a trigger's.
    public Zone zone = Zone::None;
    // The mouse's motion since the last hand-off, and since Output's last frame.
    public float32 moved = 0.0;
    public float32 shown = 0.0;
    // A press a chord or a sequence took for itself, which this source does not see until it lets go.
    public bool hidden = false;
    // The value entry whose chord gates it, -1 for none.
    public isize gate = -1;

    public ctor make(Device device, SampleKind kind, int32 control, bool flip) {
        this.device = device;
        this.kind = kind;
        this.control = control;
        this.flip = flip;
    }
}

// One device's entry of a value action: its kind and its index there, its shape, whether it is the mouse's motion, its
// parts' sources, part k's from `firsts[k]` up to `firsts[k + 1]` in the binder's sources, and its filters, from
// `filterFrom` up to `filterTo` in the binder's.
type value Entry {
    public ActionKind kind;
    public int32 action;
    public Shape shape;
    public bool motion = false;
    public InlineArray<isize>#(7) firsts;
    public isize filterFrom = 0;
    public isize filterTo = 0;
    // Its chord's modifiers, `modifiers[gateFrom]` up to `gateTo`, every one held for its value to count.
    public isize gateFrom = 0;
    public isize gateTo = 0;

    public ctor make(ActionKind kind, int32 action, Shape shape) {
        this.kind = kind;
        this.action = action;
        this.shape = shape;
        this.firsts = [0; 7];
    }
}

type resource Binder implements InputSource {
    int32 playerCount;
    int32 digitalCount;
    float32 stepSeconds;
    // Every digital action's controls, action by action: action a's are `controls[firsts[a]]` up to `controls[firsts[a + 1]]`.
    DynamicArray<Bound> controls = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<isize> firsts = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Each digital action's combined state as of the last sample handed off, and a tap's release owed to the next step.
    DynamicArray<bool> combined = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> owedRelease = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Every digital action's entries, action by action (action a's are `digitalEntries[entryFirsts[a]]` up to
    // `entryFirsts[a + 1]`), each entry's gestures, and the changes `delay`s hold back.
    DynamicArray<DigitalEntry> digitalEntries = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<isize> entryFirsts = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Gesture> gestures = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Pending> pending = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Every chord's and sequence's modifiers and steps; the digital actions' names; and the order the actions are settled
    // in, each after every action its chords and sequences hold.
    DynamicArray<Modifier> modifiers = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<string> actionNames = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<int32> actionOrder = DynamicArray.empty();
    // The `input` record's gestures' default times, in seconds.
    GestureTimes times = GestureTimes.make();
    // Every value action's entries, and the controls they read.
    DynamicArray<Entry> entries = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Source> sources = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Every value entry's filters, every curve's points in pairs (in, out), and each `smooth`'s value so far on the
    // steps' path and on Output's, by filter.
    DynamicArray<FilterRecord> filters = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<float32> points = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Vec3> smoothSteps = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Vec3> smoothShown = DynamicArray.empty();
    // The `input` record's dead zones, where it names them.
    Optional<FilterRecord> stickZone = Optional::None;
    Optional<FilterRecord> triggerZone = Optional::None;
    Optional<FilterRecord> stickPress = Optional::None;
    // Which value actions are deltas, by kind, as the game's `ActionList` says.
    DynamicArray<bool> analogDeltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> vector2Deltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> vector3Deltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    // The pad player 1 has locked in, NO_PAD while none, and player 1's active scheme.
    int32 lockSlot = NO_PAD;
    Scheme schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
    // The samples handed in, oldest first, those before `head` handed off; cleared once all are.
    DynamicArray<Sample> waiting = DynamicArray.empty();
    isize head = 0;
    // Each digital action's edges inside the step being handed off.
    DynamicArray<bool> onEdge = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> offEdge = DynamicArray.empty();
    Handoff out;
    // What Output reads, and the seconds a held control counts for in a delta: the step's, or Output's frame's.
    Handoff view;
    float32 seconds = 0.0;

    // A binder for `players` players and the game's actions, each kind's named in the generated order, bound by
    // `bindings`, every content layer's merged, with `input`'s defaults; `hz` the base rate, whose step's seconds a
    // control held counts for in a delta. A binding naming no action, a control that names none of its device's, an
    // entry its action's kind cannot read, a filter or a default out of its range, or what KYR-54 does not read yet is
    // refused, every one at once.
    public ctor Result<Binder, BindingError> make(int32 players, const ref ActionList actions,
                                                  const ref SortedMap<string, BindingRecord> bindings,
                                                  const ref InputRecord input, int32 hz) {
        this.playerCount = players;
        this.digitalCount = actions.digitalCount();
        this.stepSeconds = Time::dtAt(hz: hz);
        this.out = Handoff.make(players: players, actions: actions);
        foreach (const ref string n in actions.digitalNames().iterConst()) { this.actionNames.add(item: copy n); }
        this.view = Handoff.make(players: players, actions: actions);
        BindingError no = BindingError.make();
        DynamicArray<float32> noPoints = DynamicArray.empty();
        match (input.stickDeadZone()) {
            case Some(value: f): {
                string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: noPoints, motion: false);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { this.stickZone = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                else { no.add(line: "the `input` record's `stickDeadZone` " + why); }
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        match (input.triggerDeadZone()) {
            case Some(value: f): {
                string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: noPoints, motion: false);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { this.triggerZone = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                else { no.add(line: "the `input` record's `triggerDeadZone` " + why); }
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        match (input.stickThreshold()) {
            case Some(value: f): {
                string why = thresholdRefusal(f: f);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { this.stickPress = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                else { no.add(line: "the `input` record's `stickThreshold` " + why); }
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        this.times = input.gestureTimes();
        refuseTime(part: "hold", seconds: this.times.hold, no: no);
        refuseTime(part: "tap", seconds: this.times.tap, no: no);
        refuseTime(part: "longTap", seconds: this.times.longTap, no: no);
        refuseTime(part: "gap", seconds: this.times.gap, no: no);
        refuseTime(part: "repeatDelay", seconds: this.times.repeatDelay, no: no);
        refuseTime(part: "repeatEvery", seconds: this.times.repeatEvery, no: no);
        foreach (string action in bindings) {
            string kind = kindOf(actions: actions, name: action);
            if (kind.isEmpty()) {
                no.add(line: "the bindings of `" + action + "` name no action: an action is declared in a module's records file");
            } else if (kind == "Pose") {
                no.add(line: "the bindings of `" + action + "` bind a `Pose` action, which no device binds until XR brings one (KYR-34)");
            }
        }
        foreach (const ref string action in actions.digitalNames().iterConst()) {
            this.firsts.add(item: this.controls.length());
            this.entryFirsts.add(item: this.digitalEntries.length());
            this.combined.add(item: false);
            this.owedRelease.add(item: false);
            this.onEdge.add(item: false);
            this.offEdge.add(item: false);
            if (!bindings.contains(key: action)) { continue; }
            borrow bindings.getRef(key: action) as b {
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Keyboard, entry: b.keyboard(), no: no);
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Mouse, entry: b.mouse(), no: no);
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Gamepad, entry: b.gamepad(), no: no);
            }
        }
        this.firsts.add(item: this.controls.length());
        this.entryFirsts.add(item: this.digitalEntries.length());
        int32 a = 0;
        while (a < actions.analogCount()) {
            bool delta = actions.analogDelta(action: a);
            this.analogDeltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Analog, index: a, name: actions.analogNames()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < actions.vector2Count()) {
            bool delta = actions.vector2Delta(action: a);
            this.vector2Deltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Vector2, index: a, name: actions.vector2Names()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < actions.vector3Count()) {
            bool delta = actions.vector3Delta(action: a);
            this.vector3Deltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Vector3, index: a, name: actions.vector3Names()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        this.orderActions(no: no);
        if (no.any()) { return Result::Err(error: give no); }
        return Result::Ok(value: give this);
    }

    public const fn int32 players() { return this.playerCount; }
    public const fn int32 digitalActions() { return this.digitalCount; }
    // Player 1's active scheme as of the samples handed off.
    public const fn Scheme scheme() { return this.schemeNow; }
    // The pad slot player 1 has locked in, None while none is.
    public const fn Optional<int32> lockedPad() {
        if (this.lockSlot == NO_PAD) { return Optional::None; }
        return Optional::Some(value: this.lockSlot);
    }
    // How many controls digital action `action` is bound to, for a test to read what was bound.
    public const fn isize boundCount(int32 action) {
        if (action < 0 || action >= this.digitalCount) { return 0; }
        isize a = cast<isize>(action);
        return this.firsts[a + 1] - this.firsts[a];
    }
    // How many entries the value actions have, and how many controls they read, for a test to read what was bound.
    public const fn isize valueEntries() { return this.entries.length(); }
    public const fn isize valueSources() { return this.sources.length(); }

    // The samples a platform handed in since the last call, which arrived in the order of their times.
    public fn void take(const ref DynamicArray<Sample> samples) {
        foreach (Sample s in samples) { this.waiting.add(item: s); }
    }

    // The hand-off of a step, from the samples that arrived by `until` (inclusive, on the frame timestamp's base) and
    // were not handed off yet; the driver hands the frame's last owed step everything that arrived.
    public fn const ref Handoff handoff(int64 index, int64 until) {
        this.out.clear();
        int32 a = 0;
        while (this.head < this.waiting.length() && this.waiting[this.head].at <= until) {
            Sample s = this.waiting[this.head];
            this.apply(s: s);
            this.head = this.head + 1;
        }
        if (this.head == this.waiting.length()) {
            this.waiting.clear();
            this.head = 0;
        }
        this.advance(to: until);
        a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            isize i = cast<isize>(a);
            bool now = this.combined[i];
            Digital d = Digital.off();
            if (this.owedRelease[i]) {
                d.released = true;
                this.owedRelease[i] = false;
            }
            if (this.onEdge[i]) {
                d.pressed = true;
                d.held = true;
                if (!now) { this.owedRelease[i] = true; }
                if (this.offEdge[i] && now) { d.released = true; }
            } else if (this.offEdge[i]) {
                d.released = true;
            } else {
                d.held = now;
            }
            d.progress = d.held ? 1.0 : this.progressOf(action: a, at: until);
            if (this.playerCount >= 1) { this.out.setDigital(player: 1, action: a, value: d); }
            a = a + 1;
        }
        if (this.playerCount >= 1) {
            this.seconds = this.stepSeconds;
            this.handValues(forOutput: false);
            this.out.setScheme(player: 1, value: this.schemeNow);
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            this.onEdge[cast<isize>(a)] = false;
            this.offEdge[cast<isize>(a)] = false;
            a = a + 1;
        }
        isize k = 0;
        while (k < this.sources.length()) {
            this.sources[k].moved = 0.0;
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return this.out;
    }

    // What Output reads this frame: every sample taken so far applied, each state as of the newest, each delta since
    // the last call at `seconds`, the frame's, every digital off; the samples' edges and motion kept for the next step.
    public fn const ref Handoff newest(float32 seconds) {
        this.view.clear();
        while (this.head < this.waiting.length()) {
            Sample s = this.waiting[this.head];
            this.apply(s: s);
            this.head = this.head + 1;
        }
        this.waiting.clear();
        this.head = 0;
        if (this.playerCount >= 1) {
            this.seconds = seconds;
            this.handValues(forOutput: true);
            this.view.setScheme(player: 1, value: this.schemeNow);
        }
        isize k = 0;
        while (k < this.sources.length()) {
            this.sources[k].shown = 0.0;
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return this.view;
    }

    // Each value action's value into player 1's hand-off, a step's or Output's: a state's most actuated entry, a
    // delta's sum, a control held counting for `this.seconds`.
    fn void handValues(bool forOutput) {
        isize e = 0;
        while (e < this.entries.length()) {
            Entry entry = this.entries[e];
            if (!entry.motion && !this.allOn(from: entry.gateFrom, to: entry.gateTo)) {
                e = e + 1;
                continue;
            }
            Vec3 parts = this.entryValue(e: entry, forOutput: forOutput);
            Vec3 v = this.filtered(e: entry, value: parts, forOutput: forOutput);
            bool delta = this.isDelta(kind: entry.kind, action: entry.action);
            if (delta && !entry.motion) {
                v = Vec3.of(x: v.x * this.seconds, y: v.y * this.seconds, z: v.z * this.seconds);
            }
            match (entry.kind) {
                case Analog: {
                    float32 had = forOutput ? this.view.analog(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.analog(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    float32 now = delta ? had + v.x : (absOf(x: v.x) > absOf(x: had) ? v.x : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setAnalog(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setAnalog(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case Vector2: {
                    Vec2 had = forOutput ? this.view.vector2(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.vector2(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    Vec2 mine = Vec2.of(x: v.x, y: v.y);
                    Vec2 now = delta ? had + mine : (v.x * v.x + v.y * v.y > had.x * had.x + had.y * had.y ? mine : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setVector2(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setVector2(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case Vector3: {
                    Vec3 had = forOutput ? this.view.vector3(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.vector3(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    Vec3 now = delta ? had + v : (lengthSquared(v: v) > lengthSquared(v: had) ? v : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setVector3(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setVector3(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case _: { }
            };
            e = e + 1;
        }
    }

    // An entry's value through its filters, in the order written, each on the axes its kind reads (an `Analog` 1, a
    // `Vector2` 2, a `Vector3` 3), the others held at 0.
    fn Vec3 filtered(Entry e, Vec3 value, bool forOutput) {
        int32 dims = match (e.kind) { case Analog: 1; case Vector2: 2; case _: 3; };
        Vec3 v = value;
        isize i = e.filterFrom;
        while (i < e.filterTo) {
            FilterRecord f = this.filters[i];
            match (f.kind) {
                case DeadZone: { v = deadZoned(v: v, f: f); }
                case Scale: { v = Vec3.of(x: v.x * f.a, y: v.y * f.b, z: v.z * f.c); }
                case Invert: { v = Vec3.of(x: invertedBy(x: v.x, by: f.a), y: invertedBy(x: v.y, by: f.b), z: invertedBy(x: v.z, by: f.c)); }
                case Curve: {
                    if (f.points) {
                        v = Vec3.of(x: this.throughPoints(x: v.x, f: f), y: this.throughPoints(x: v.y, f: f),
                                    z: this.throughPoints(x: v.z, f: f));
                    } else {
                        v = Vec3.of(x: powered(x: v.x, e: f.a), y: powered(x: v.y, e: f.b), z: powered(x: v.z, e: f.c));
                    }
                }
                case Clamp: { v = clampedBy(v: v, f: f); }
                case Remap: { v = Vec3.of(x: remapped(x: v.x, f: f), y: remapped(x: v.y, f: f), z: remapped(x: v.z, f: f)); }
                case Normalize: { if (f.on) { v = unit(v: v); } }
                case Digital: { if (f.on) { v = Vec3.of(x: signOf(x: v.x), y: signOf(x: v.y), z: signOf(x: v.z)); } }
                case Smooth: { v = this.smoothed(i: i, v: v, f: f, motion: e.motion, forOutput: forOutput); }
                case Threshold: { }
            };
            v = masked(v: v, dims: dims);
            i = i + 1;
        }
        return v;
    }

    // A curve through `f`'s points on `x`'s size, linear between them and level past the ends, its sign kept.
    const fn float32 throughPoints(float32 x, FilterRecord f) {
        float32 a = absOf(x: x);
        isize first = f.pointsFrom;
        isize last = f.pointsTo - 2;
        float32 got = this.points[first + 1];
        if (a >= this.points[last]) {
            got = this.points[last + 1];
        } else if (a > this.points[first]) {
            isize k = first;
            while (k < last) {
                float32 x0 = this.points[k];
                float32 x1 = this.points[k + 2];
                if (a <= x1) {
                    float32 y0 = this.points[k + 1];
                    float32 y1 = this.points[k + 3];
                    got = y0 + (a - x0) / (x1 - x0) * (y1 - y0);
                    k = last;
                } else {
                    k = k + 2;
                }
            }
        }
        return x < 0.0 ? 0.0 - got : (x > 0.0 ? got : 0.0);
    }

    // `v` smoothed by `f`'s time: moved toward its value by the share of it `this.seconds` makes, from the path's last
    // value; the mouse's motion as a speed, so how far it moves is kept whatever the step.
    fn Vec3 smoothed(isize i, Vec3 v, FilterRecord f, bool motion, bool forOutput) {
        float32 dt = this.seconds;
        Vec3 had = forOutput ? this.smoothShown[i] : this.smoothSteps[i];
        if (dt <= 0.0) { return motion ? v : had; }
        float32 share = 1.0 - exp(x: 0.0 - dt / f.a);
        Vec3 target = motion ? Vec3.of(x: v.x / dt, y: v.y / dt, z: v.z / dt) : v;
        Vec3 now = Vec3.of(x: had.x + (target.x - had.x) * share, y: had.y + (target.y - had.y) * share,
                           z: had.z + (target.z - had.z) * share);
        if (forOutput) { this.smoothShown[i] = now; } else { this.smoothSteps[i] = now; }
        return motion ? Vec3.of(x: now.x * dt, y: now.y * dt, z: now.z * dt) : now;
    }

    const fn bool isDelta(ActionKind kind, int32 action) {
        isize a = cast<isize>(action);
        return match (kind) {
            case Analog: this.analogDeltas[a];
            case Vector2: this.vector2Deltas[a];
            case Vector3: this.vector3Deltas[a];
            case _: false;
        };
    }

    // An entry's value from its parts, as a three-component value (an `Analog` its x, a `Vector2` its x and y); the
    // mouse's motion since the last step, or since Output's last frame.
    const fn Vec3 entryValue(Entry e, bool forOutput) {
        float32 p0 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 0, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p1 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 1, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p2 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 2, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p3 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 3, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p4 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 4, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p5 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 5, forOutput: forOutput);
        return match (e.shape) {
            case One: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: 0.0, z: 0.0);
            case Pair: Vec3.of(x: p0 - p1, y: 0.0, z: 0.0);
            case Keys2: clamped(v: Vec3.of(x: p3 - p2, y: p0 - p1, z: 0.0));
            case Axes2: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: p1, z: 0.0);
            case Keys3: clamped(v: Vec3.of(x: p3 - p2, y: p0 - p1, z: p5 - p4));
            case Axes3: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: p1, z: p2);
        };
    }

    // A part's value: the mouse's motion summed, or the most actuated of its controls.
    const fn float32 partValue(Entry e, int32 part, bool forOutput) {
        isize from = e.firsts[cast<isize>(part)];
        isize to = e.firsts[cast<isize>(part) + 1];
        float32 best = 0.0;
        isize i = from;
        while (i < to) {
            Source s = this.sources[i];
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Motion) { best = best + (forOutput ? s.shown : s.moved); }
            else {
                float32 v = this.zonedSource(s: s);
                if (absOf(x: v) > absOf(x: best)) { best = v; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        return best;
    }

    // A source's value through its default dead zone, on its own axis.
    const fn float32 zonedSource(Source s) { return this.made(v: s.value, zone: s.zone, half: s.half); }

    // One sample: every gesture's deadline before it, then a pad's lock, then each control it moves, then each digital
    // action whose combined state it changes.
    fn void apply(Sample s) {
        this.advance(to: s.at);
        match (s.kind) {
            case Connected: { return; }
            case Disconnected: {
                if (s.slot == this.lockSlot) {
                    this.lockSlot = NO_PAD;
                    this.release(device: Device::Gamepad, t: s.at);
                    this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
                }
                return;
            }
            case Control: { }
            case Travel: {
                if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
                if (s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
                this.setValues(s: s);
                this.moveButtons(s: s);
                return;
            }
            case Axis: {
                if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
                if (absOf(x: s.value) >= STICK_IN_USE) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
                this.setValues(s: s);
                this.moveButtons(s: s);
                return;
            }
            case Motion: {
                this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
                this.setValues(s: s);
                return;
            }
        };
        bool on = s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt;
        if (s.device == Device::Gamepad) {
            if (this.lockSlot == NO_PAD && on) { this.lockSlot = s.slot; }
            if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
            if (on) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
        } else if (on) {
            this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
        }
        if (on) { this.maskFor(s: s); }
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.controls.length()) {
            if (this.controls[i].device == s.device && this.controls[i].kind == SampleKind::Control && this.controls[i].control == s.control) {
                this.controls[i].on = on && !this.controls[i].hidden;
                if (!on) { this.controls[i].hidden = false; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        this.setValues(s: s);
        this.settle(t: s.at);
    }

    // Each value made a button the sample moves: on at its press point, off at its release point or below, each digital
    // action's combined state settled where one changed.
    fn void moveButtons(Sample s) {
        bool moved = false;
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.controls.length()) {
            Bound c = this.controls[i];
            if (c.device == s.device && c.kind == s.kind && c.control == s.control) {
                float32 v = this.made(v: c.flip ? 0.0 - s.value : s.value, zone: c.zone, half: c.half);
                bool on = c.on ? v > c.release : v >= c.press;
                if (on != c.on) {
                    this.controls[i].on = on;
                    moved = true;
                }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        if (moved) { this.settle(t: s.at); }
    }

    // A pad value through its default dead zone, on its own axis, then the half of it a stick's direction reads.
    const fn float32 made(float32 v, Zone zone, float32 half) {
        Optional<FilterRecord> f = match (zone) {
            case None: Optional::None;
            case Stick: this.stickZone;
            case Trigger: this.triggerZone;
        };
        float32 z = match (f) {
            case Some(value: d): signOf(x: v) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v), f: d);
            case None: v;
        };
        if (half > 0.0) { return z > 0.0 ? z : 0.0; }
        if (half < 0.0) { return z < 0.0 ? 0.0 - z : 0.0; }
        return z;
    }

    // Each value source the sample moves: an edge's 1 or 0, a travel or an axis as it reads (a Y turned over), or the
    // mouse's motion added to what it moved this step.
    fn void setValues(Sample s) {
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            Source src = this.sources[i];
            if (src.device == s.device && src.kind == s.kind && src.control == s.control) {
                float32 v = s.value;
                if (s.kind == SampleKind::Control) {
                    bool down = s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt;
                    v = down && !src.hidden ? 1.0 : 0.0;
                    if (!down) { this.sources[i].hidden = false; }
                }
                if (src.flip) { v = -v; }
                if (s.kind == SampleKind::Motion) {
                    if (src.gate < 0 || this.gateOn(entry: src.gate)) {
                        this.sources[i].moved = src.moved + v;
                        this.sources[i].shown = src.shown + v;
                    }
                }
                else { this.sources[i].value = v; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // Every control of `device` off and at rest: a pad gone with its lock.
    fn void release(Device device, int64 t) {
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.controls.length()) {
            if (this.controls[i].device == device) { this.controls[i].on = false; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        i = 0;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            if (this.sources[i].device == device) { this.sources[i].value = 0.0; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        this.settle(t: t);
    }

    // Each digital entry's controls at `t`: where whether any is on changed, its first gesture takes the change, or the
    // action, where it has none.
    fn void settle(int64 t) {
        isize o = 0;
        while (o < this.actionOrder.length()) {
            isize ai = cast<isize>(this.actionOrder[o]);
            isize e = this.entryFirsts[ai];
            while (e < this.entryFirsts[ai + 1]) {
                DigitalEntry de = this.digitalEntries[e];
                bool any = false;
                isize c = de.from;
                while (c < de.to) {
                    if (this.controls[c].on) { any = true; }
                    c = c + 1;
                }
                if (any != de.raw) {
                    this.digitalEntries[e].raw = any;
                    this.feed(e: e, g: de.gestureFrom, change: any ? Change::On : Change::Off, t: t);
                }
                e = e + 1;
            }
            o = o + 1;
        }
        this.recheck(t: t);
    }

    // Whether modifier `m` is held: its action on, or any control of its group.
    const fn bool modifierOn(isize m) {
        Modifier x = this.modifiers[m];
        if (x.action >= 0) { return this.combined[cast<isize>(x.action)]; }
        isize c = x.from;
        while (c < x.to) {
            if (this.controls[c].on) { return true; }
            c = c + 1;
        }
        return false;
    }

    // Whether modifiers `from` up to `to` are all held: none is, vacuously.
    const fn bool allOn(isize from, isize to) {
        isize m = from;
        while (m < to) {
            if (!this.modifierOn(m: m)) { return false; }
            m = m + 1;
        }
        return true;
    }

    // Every modifier and step looked at again after a change at `t`: a chord whose modifier let go lets go, and a
    // sequence's step pressed moves it on; again until nothing changes, since a chord letting go may let go of an action
    // another chord holds.
    fn void recheck(int64 t) {
        bool changed = true;
        while (changed) {
            changed = false;
            isize m = 0;
            while (m < this.modifiers.length()) {
                bool now = this.modifierOn(m: m);
                Modifier x = this.modifiers[m];
                if (now != x.was) {
                    this.modifiers[m].was = now;
                    changed = true;
                    if (x.gesture >= 0) { this.modifierMoved(g: x.gesture, step: x.step, rose: now, t: t); }
                }
                m = m + 1;
            }
        }
    }

    // A modifier or a step of gesture `g` held (`rose`) or let go at `t`. A chord lets go when one of its modifiers does.
    // A sequence takes the step it waits for, or its first step again; one press moves it once.
    fn void modifierMoved(isize g, int32 step, bool rose, int64 t) {
        Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
        isize e = x.entry;
        match (x.kind) {
            case Chord: {
                if (!rose && x.out) {
                    this.gestures[g].out = false;
                    this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
                }
            }
            case Sequence: {
                if (rose && x.tookAt != t) {
                    int32 next = -1;
                    if (step == x.taps && x.taps < x.count) { next = x.taps + 1; }
                    else if (step == 0) { next = 1; }
                    if (next > 0) {
                        this.gestures[g].taps = next;
                        this.gestures[g].tookAt = t;
                        this.gestures[g].due = later(t: t, by: x.a + 1);
                    }
                }
            }
            case _: { }
        };
    }

    // A press a chord or a sequence takes for itself (design/input.md § Decided, 2026-11-24, question 3): where a digital
    // entry reading `s`'s control has a masking chord whose modifiers are all held, or a masking sequence whose steps all
    // came, every other entry reading it is masked from this press until it lets go, a value's part included.
    fn void maskFor(Sample s) {
        bool any = false;
        isize e = 0;
        while (e < this.digitalEntries.length()) {
            if (this.claims(e: e, s: s)) { any = true; }
            e = e + 1;
        }
        if (!any) { return; }
        e = 0;
        while (e < this.digitalEntries.length()) {
            if (!this.claims(e: e, s: s)) {
                DigitalEntry de = this.digitalEntries[e];
                isize c = de.from;
                while (c < de.to) {
                    if (this.controls[c].device == s.device && this.controls[c].kind == SampleKind::Control && this.controls[c].control == s.control) {
                        this.controls[c].hidden = true;
                    }
                    c = c + 1;
                }
            }
            e = e + 1;
        }
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            if (this.sources[i].device == s.device && this.sources[i].kind == SampleKind::Control && this.sources[i].control == s.control) {
                this.sources[i].hidden = true;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // Whether digital entry `e` takes a press of `s`'s control for itself: it reads the control, and a masking chord of
    // its holds every modifier, or a masking sequence of its has every step.
    const fn bool claims(isize e, Sample s) {
        DigitalEntry de = this.digitalEntries[e];
        bool reads = false;
        isize c = de.from;
        while (c < de.to) {
            if (this.controls[c].device == s.device && this.controls[c].kind == SampleKind::Control && this.controls[c].control == s.control) {
                reads = true;
            }
            c = c + 1;
        }
        if (!reads) { return false; }
        isize g = de.gestureFrom;
        while (g < de.gestureTo) {
            Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
            if (x.masks && x.kind == GestureKind::Chord && this.allOn(from: x.modFrom, to: x.modTo)) { return true; }
            if (x.masks && x.kind == GestureKind::Sequence && x.taps >= x.count) { return true; }
            g = g + 1;
        }
        return false;
    }

    // The digital actions in the order they are settled, each after every action its chords and sequences hold; a circle
    // of actions holding each other refused, naming it.
    fn void orderActions(ref BindingError no) {
        DynamicArray<int32> state = DynamicArray.empty();
        DynamicArray<int32> parent = DynamicArray.empty();
        int32 a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            state.add(item: 0);
            parent.add(item: -1);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            if (state[cast<isize>(a)] == 0) {
                bool fine = this.visit(a: a, state: state, parent: parent, no: no);
                if (!fine) { return; }
            }
            a = a + 1;
        }
    }

    // Action `a` and every action its chords and sequences hold, depth first: false, the circle refused, where one holds
    // an action still being visited. `state` is 0 unvisited, 1 under way, 2 done.
    fn bool visit(int32 a, ref DynamicArray<int32> state, ref DynamicArray<int32> parent, ref BindingError no) {
        isize ai = cast<isize>(a);
        state[ai] = 1;
        isize k = this.entryFirsts[ai];
        while (k < this.entryFirsts[ai + 1]) {
            DigitalEntry de = this.digitalEntries[k];
            isize g = de.gestureFrom;
            while (g < de.gestureTo) {
                Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
                isize m = x.modFrom;
                while (m < x.modTo) {
                    int32 b = this.modifiers[m].action;
                    if (b >= 0) {
                        int32 seen = state[cast<isize>(b)];
                        if (seen == 1) {
                            string loop = "`" + this.actionNames[cast<isize>(b)] + "`";
                            int32 at = a;
                            string back = "";
                            while (at != b && at >= 0) {
                                back = " -> `" + this.actionNames[cast<isize>(at)] + "`" + back;
                                at = parent[cast<isize>(at)];
                            }
                            no.add(line: "the actions " + loop + back + " -> " + loop + " hold each other in their chords and sequences: one of them must be held first");
                            return false;
                        }
                        if (seen == 0) {
                            parent[cast<isize>(b)] = a;
                            if (!this.visit(a: b, state: state, parent: parent, no: no)) { return false; }
                        }
                    }
                    m = m + 1;
                }
                g = g + 1;
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        state[ai] = 2;
        this.actionOrder.add(item: a);
        return true;
    }

    // A chord's or a sequence's names into modifiers of gesture `gesture` (-1 for a value's chord, which gates it), each
    // a group of the scheme's controls or a digital action: why one is refused, or "".
    fn string takeNames(const ref ControlEntry entry, GestureRecord r, isize gesture, Device device) {
        isize k = r.namesFrom;
        while (k < r.namesTo) {
            string name = copy entry.gestureNames()[k];
            GestureName mark = entry.gestureMarks()[k];
            Modifier m = Modifier.make(gesture: gesture);
            m.step = mark.step;
            if (mark.action) {
                isize found = -1;
                isize n = 0;
                while (n < this.actionNames.length()) {
                    if (this.actionNames[n] == name) { found = n; }
                    n = n + 1;
                }
                if (found < 0) {
                    return "names the action `" + name + "` to hold, which is no `Digital` of the game's: a chord and a sequence hold a `Digital`";
                }
                m.action = cast<int32>(found);
            } else {
                m.from = this.controls.length();
                string why = this.modifierControls(name: name, device: device);
                if (!why.isEmpty()) { return why; }
                m.to = this.controls.length();
            }
            this.modifiers.add(item: m);
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return "";
    }

    // The controls a chord's or a sequence's name holds, added to the binder's, on the entry's scheme: a pad's button or a
    // stick's direction; or a key, kyoten's either-side `Shift`, `Control`, `Alt` and `Meta`, or a mouse button. Why the
    // name is refused, or "".
    fn string modifierControls(const ref string name, Device device) {
        string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
        if (device == Device::Gamepad) {
            Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give p) {
                case Ok(value: button): {
                    this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: Device::Gamepad, control: cast<int32>(button)));
                    return "";
                }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    Optional<Source> direction = stickDirection(name: name);
                    match (direction) {
                        case Some(value: d): {
                            match (this.stickPress) {
                                case Some(value: f): {
                                    Bound b = Bound.make(device: Device::Gamepad, control: d.control);
                                    b.kind = SampleKind::Axis;
                                    b.flip = d.flip;
                                    b.half = d.half;
                                    b.zone = Zone::Stick;
                                    b.press = f.a;
                                    b.release = releaseOf(f: f);
                                    this.controls.add(item: b);
                                    return "";
                                }
                                case None: {
                                    return "names `" + name + "` to hold, a stick's direction, which as a button needs the `input` record's `stickThreshold`";
                                }
                            };
                        }
                        case None: {
                            string why = e.message();
                            return "names `" + name + "` to hold, which is no gamepad control: no button (" + why + ") and no stick's direction (" + directionNames() + ")";
                        }
                    };
                }
            };
        }
        int32 left = -1;
        int32 right = -1;
        if (name == "Shift") { left = cast<int32>(Key::ShiftLeft); right = cast<int32>(Key::ShiftRight); }
        else if (name == "Control") { left = cast<int32>(Key::ControlLeft); right = cast<int32>(Key::ControlRight); }
        else if (name == "Alt") { left = cast<int32>(Key::AltLeft); right = cast<int32>(Key::AltRight); }
        else if (name == "Meta") { left = cast<int32>(Key::MetaLeft); right = cast<int32>(Key::MetaRight); }
        if (left >= 0) {
            this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: Device::Keyboard, control: left));
            this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: Device::Keyboard, control: right));
            return "";
        }
        Result<int32, Owned<Error>> k = controlOf(device: Device::Keyboard, name: name);
        match (give k) {
            case Ok(value: v): {
                this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: Device::Keyboard, control: v));
                return "";
            }
            case Err(error: e): {
                Result<int32, Owned<Error>> b = controlOf(device: Device::Mouse, name: name);
                match (give b) {
                    case Ok(value: v): {
                        this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: Device::Mouse, control: v));
                        return "";
                    }
                    case Err(error: f): {
                        string asKey = e.message();
                        return "names `" + name + "` to hold, which is no key or mouse button: " + asKey + "; nor `Shift`, `Control`, `Alt` or `Meta`, either side's";
                    }
                };
            }
        };
    }

    // What an entry's last gesture makes reaches its action: the action is on while any of its entries is, an edge
    // noted where that changed, and a press again noted while it is on.
    fn void reach(isize e, Change change) {
        match (change) {
            case On: { this.digitalEntries[e].on = true; }
            case Off: { this.digitalEntries[e].on = false; }
            case Again: { }
        };
        isize ai = cast<isize>(this.digitalEntries[e].action);
        bool any = false;
        isize k = this.entryFirsts[ai];
        while (k < this.entryFirsts[ai + 1]) {
            if (this.digitalEntries[k].on) { any = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (any != this.combined[ai]) {
            if (any) { this.onEdge[ai] = true; } else { this.offEdge[ai] = true; }
            this.combined[ai] = any;
        } else if (any && change == Change::Again) {
            this.onEdge[ai] = true;
        }
    }

    // Gesture `g` of entry `e` takes `change` at `t`, and hands what it makes to the next gesture, or past the last to
    // the action.
    fn void feed(isize e, isize g, Change change, int64 t) {
        if (g >= this.digitalEntries[e].gestureTo) {
            this.reach(e: e, change: change);
            return;
        }
        Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
        match (x.kind) {
            case Hold: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        this.gestures[g].since = t;
                        this.gestures[g].due = later(t: t, by: x.a);
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        this.gestures[g].out = false;
                        this.gestures[g].due = NOT_DUE;
                        if (x.out) { this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t); }
                    }
                    case Again: { if (x.out) { this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t); } }
                };
            }
            case Tap: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        this.gestures[g].since = t;
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        if (t - x.since <= x.a) { this.pulse(e: e, g: g, t: t); }
                    }
                    case Again: { }
                };
            }
            case LongTap: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        this.gestures[g].since = t;
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        if (t - x.since >= x.a) { this.pulse(e: e, g: g, t: t); }
                    }
                    case Again: { }
                };
            }
            case MultiTap: {
                bool press = change == Change::On || (change == Change::Again && !x.out);
                if (press) {
                    int32 counted = x.taps + 1;
                    this.gestures[g].input = true;
                    this.gestures[g].since = t;
                    if (counted >= x.count) {
                        this.gestures[g].taps = 0;
                        this.gestures[g].out = true;
                        this.gestures[g].due = NOT_DUE;
                        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
                    } else {
                        this.gestures[g].taps = counted;
                        this.gestures[g].due = later(t: t, by: x.a + 1);
                    }
                } else if (change == Change::Again) {
                    this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t);
                } else {
                    this.gestures[g].input = false;
                    if (x.out) {
                        this.gestures[g].out = false;
                        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
                    } else if (x.taps > 0) {
                        this.gestures[g].due = later(t: t, by: x.b + 1);
                    }
                }
            }
            case Repeat: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        this.gestures[g].out = true;
                        this.gestures[g].taps = 1;
                        this.gestures[g].due = x.count == 0 || x.count > 1 ? later(t: t, by: x.a) : NOT_DUE;
                        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        this.gestures[g].out = false;
                        this.gestures[g].due = NOT_DUE;
                        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
                    }
                    case Again: { this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t); }
                };
            }
            case Toggle: {
                if (!x.enabled) {
                    this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: change, t: t);
                } else if (change != Change::Off) {
                    bool flipped = !x.out;
                    this.gestures[g].out = flipped;
                    this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: flipped ? Change::On : Change::Off, t: t);
                }
            }
            case Delay: {
                int64 by = change == Change::Off ? x.b : x.a;
                int64 at = later(t: t, by: by);
                if (at < x.queuedTo) { at = x.queuedTo; }
                this.gestures[g].queuedTo = at;
                this.pending.add(item: Pending.make(gesture: g, at: at, change: change));
                if (x.due == NOT_DUE) { this.gestures[g].due = at; }
            }
            case Chord: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        if (this.allOn(from: x.modFrom, to: x.modTo)) {
                            this.gestures[g].out = true;
                            this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
                        }
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        if (x.out) {
                            this.gestures[g].out = false;
                            this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
                        }
                    }
                    case Again: { if (x.out) { this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t); } }
                };
            }
            case Sequence: {
                match (change) {
                    case On: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = true;
                        if (x.taps >= x.count) {
                            this.gestures[g].taps = 0;
                            this.gestures[g].due = NOT_DUE;
                            this.gestures[g].tookAt = t;
                            this.gestures[g].out = true;
                            this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
                        }
                    }
                    case Off: {
                        this.gestures[g].input = false;
                        if (x.out) {
                            this.gestures[g].out = false;
                            this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
                        }
                    }
                    case Again: { if (x.out) { this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t); } }
                };
            }
            case _: { }
        };
    }

    // A press for one step from gesture `g`: on, then off at the same moment, which the action shows pressed and held
    // that step and released the next.
    fn void pulse(isize e, isize g, int64 t) {
        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
        this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Off, t: t);
    }

    // Every gesture's deadline up to `to`, inclusive, the earliest first, each at its own time.
    fn void advance(int64 to) {
        bool more = true;
        while (more) {
            isize next = -1;
            int64 when = NOT_DUE;
            isize g = 0;
            while (g < this.gestures.length()) {
                if (this.gestures[g].due < when) {
                    when = this.gestures[g].due;
                    next = g;
                }
                g = g + 1;
            }
            if (next < 0 || when > to) { more = false; }
            else {
                this.fire(g: next, t: when, to: to);
                this.recheck(t: when);
            }
        }
    }

    // Gesture `g`'s deadline at `t`, inside a call that reaches `to`:
    // - a `hold` held its time turns on (one let go has no deadline);
    // - a `multiTap` whose press was held too long, or whose next press did not come within its gap, starts again;
    // - a `repeat` presses again, and waits for its next from then; one that fell behind (a long frame) presses once,
    //   then waits a whole interval from `to`, so it never catches up, as the-mallow-man's menus and Unity's UI do;
    // - a `delay` hands on the change it held back longest.
    fn void fire(isize g, int64 t, int64 to) {
        Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
        this.gestures[g].due = NOT_DUE;
        isize e = x.entry;
        match (x.kind) {
            case Hold: {
                this.gestures[g].out = true;
                this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::On, t: t);
            }
            case MultiTap: { this.gestures[g].taps = 0; }
            case Sequence: { this.gestures[g].taps = 0; }
            case Repeat: {
                int32 made = x.taps + 1;
                this.gestures[g].taps = made;
                if (x.count == 0 || made < x.count) {
                    int64 next = later(t: t, by: x.b);
                    if (next <= to) { next = later(t: to, by: x.b); }
                    this.gestures[g].due = next;
                }
                this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: Change::Again, t: t);
            }
            case Delay: {
                isize i = 0;
                bool handed = false;
                Change change = Change::Off;
                int64 nextDue = NOT_DUE;
                while (i < this.pending.length()) {
                    Pending p = this.pending[i];
                    if (p.gesture == g && !p.done) {
                        if (!handed) {
                            this.pending[i].done = true;
                            change = p.change;
                            handed = true;
                        } else if (nextDue == NOT_DUE) {
                            nextDue = p.at;
                        }
                    }
                    i = i + 1;
                }
                this.gestures[g].due = nextDue;
                bool all = true;
                foreach (Pending p in this.pending) { if (!p.done) { all = false; } }
                if (all) { this.pending.clear(); }
                if (handed) {
                    if (change == Change::On) { this.gestures[g].out = true; }
                    if (change == Change::Off) { this.gestures[g].out = false; }
                    this.feed(e: e, g: g + 1, change: change, t: t);
                }
            }
            case _: { }
        };
    }

    // Whether value entry `entry`'s chord holds every modifier: an entry with none, always.
    const fn bool gateOn(isize entry) {
        Entry x = this.entries[entry];
        return this.allOn(from: x.gateFrom, to: x.gateTo);
    }

    // How far digital action `action`'s gesture under way has come at `at`: the most of its entries'.
    const fn float32 progressOf(int32 action, int64 at) {
        isize ai = cast<isize>(action);
        float32 most = 0.0;
        isize k = this.entryFirsts[ai];
        while (k < this.entryFirsts[ai + 1]) {
            float32 p = this.entryProgress(e: k, at: at);
            if (p > most) { most = p; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return most;
    }

    // An entry's progress, while it is off (one on makes its action held, whose progress is 1): that of the gesture
    // nearest its end that is under way.
    const fn float32 entryProgress(isize e, int64 at) {
        DigitalEntry de = this.digitalEntries[e];
        isize g = de.gestureTo - 1;
        while (g >= de.gestureFrom) {
            float32 p = this.gestureProgress(g: g, at: at);
            if (p > 0.0) { return p; }
            g = g - 1;
        }
        return 0.0;
    }

    // One gesture's progress: a `hold`'s or a `longTap`'s share of its time held, a `multiTap`'s presses counted of its
    // count, and 1 while any gesture makes on.
    const fn float32 gestureProgress(isize g, int64 at) {
        Gesture x = this.gestures[g];
        if (x.out) { return 1.0; }
        return match (x.kind) {
            case Hold: x.input ? shareOf(from: x.since, to: at, of: x.a) : 0.0;
            case LongTap: x.input ? shareOf(from: x.since, to: at, of: x.a) : 0.0;
            case MultiTap: x.taps > 0 ? cast<float32>(x.taps) / cast<float32>(x.count) : 0.0;
            case Sequence: x.taps > 0 ? cast<float32>(x.taps) / cast<float32>(x.count + 1) : 0.0;
            case _: 0.0;
        };
    }

    // An entry's gestures into the binder's, each held to its range, its times its own or the `input` record's: false,
    // with every refusal added, when any is refused.
    fn bool takeGestures(const ref ControlEntry entry, isize at, Device device, const ref string whose, ref BindingError no) {
        bool fine = true;
        foreach (const ref GestureRecord read in entry.gestures().iterConst()) {
            GestureRecord r = read;
            Gesture g = Gesture.make(kind: r.kind, entry: at);
            string word = gestureWord(kind: r.kind);
            string why = "";
            match (r.kind) {
                case Hold: { g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.hold, word: word, part: "hold", why: why); }
                case Tap: { g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.tap, word: word, part: "tap", why: why); }
                case LongTap: {
                    g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.longTap, word: word, part: "longTap", why: why);
                }
                case MultiTap: {
                    g.count = r.count;
                    if (r.count < 2) { why = "lists a `multiTap` of ${r.count} taps: a multi-tap counts 2 or more"; }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) {
                        g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.tap, word: "multiTap`'s `tap", part: "tap", why: why);
                    }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) {
                        g.b = nanosFor(own: r.hasB, value: r.b, fallback: this.times.gap, word: "multiTap`'s `gap", part: "gap", why: why);
                    }
                }
                case Repeat: {
                    g.count = r.count;
                    if (r.count < 0) { why = "lists a `repeat` whose `limit` is ${r.count}: its most presses are 0, for no limit, or more"; }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) {
                        g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.repeatDelay, word: "repeat`'s `delay", part: "repeatDelay", why: why);
                    }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) {
                        g.b = nanosFor(own: r.hasB, value: r.b, fallback: this.times.repeatEvery, word: "repeat`'s `every", part: "repeatEvery", why: why);
                    }
                }
                case Toggle: { g.enabled = r.on; }
                case Delay: {
                    g.a = nanosOf(seconds: r.a, zero: true);
                    g.b = nanosOf(seconds: r.b, zero: true);
                    if (g.a < 0 || g.b < 0) {
                        why = "lists a `delay` of ${r.a} and ${r.b} seconds: a delay's `start` and `end` are 0 or more";
                    }
                }
                case Chord: {
                    g.masks = r.masks;
                    g.modFrom = this.modifiers.length();
                    if (r.namesTo == r.namesFrom) { why = "lists a `chord` holding nothing: a chord names a control or an action to hold"; }
                    else { why = this.takeNames(entry: entry, r: r, gesture: this.gestures.length(), device: device); }
                    g.modTo = this.modifiers.length();
                }
                case Sequence: {
                    g.masks = r.masks;
                    g.count = r.count;
                    g.modFrom = this.modifiers.length();
                    if (r.count == 0) { why = "lists a `sequence` of no steps: a sequence names the steps before its own control"; }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) {
                        g.a = nanosFor(own: r.hasA, value: r.a, fallback: this.times.gap, word: "sequence`'s `within", part: "gap", why: why);
                    }
                    if (why.isEmpty()) { why = this.takeNames(entry: entry, r: r, gesture: this.gestures.length(), device: device); }
                    g.modTo = this.modifiers.length();
                }
                case _: { why = "lists a `" + word + "`, which the fourth part's next commit reads"; }
            };
            if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                fine = false;
                continue;
            }
            this.gestures.add(item: g);
        }
        return fine;
    }

    // An entry naming no dead zone of its own takes the defaults: the stick's, radial, as its first filter where it
    // reads both axes of one stick as its x and y; else each stick axis and trigger it reads through its own.
    fn void zoneDefaults(Entry made, isize first) {
        bool pair = false;
        if (made.shape == Shape::Axes2 && made.firsts[1] - made.firsts[0] == 1 && made.firsts[2] - made.firsts[1] == 1) {
            Source x = this.sources[made.firsts[0]];
            Source y = this.sources[made.firsts[1]];
            pair = x.kind == SampleKind::Axis && y.kind == SampleKind::Axis && x.control / 2 == y.control / 2
                && x.control != y.control && x.half == 0.0 && y.half == 0.0;
        }
        if (pair) {
            match (this.stickZone) {
                case Some(value: f): {
                    this.filters.add(item: f);
                    this.smoothSteps.add(item: Vec3.zero());
                    this.smoothShown.add(item: Vec3.zero());
                }
                case None: { }
            };
            return;
        }
        isize i = first;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            Source s = this.sources[i];
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Axis) { this.sources[i].zone = Zone::Stick; }
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Travel && (s.control == cast<int32>(PadButton::LeftTrigger) || s.control == cast<int32>(PadButton::RightTrigger))) {
                this.sources[i].zone = Zone::Trigger;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // An entry's filters into the binder's, each held to its range: false, with every refusal added, when any is
    // refused.
    fn bool takeFilters(const ref ControlEntry entry, bool motion, const ref string whose, ref BindingError no) {
        bool fine = true;
        foreach (const ref FilterRecord read in entry.filters().iterConst()) {
            FilterRecord f = read;
            string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: entry.curvePoints(), motion: motion);
            if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                fine = false;
                continue;
            }
            if (f.points) {
                isize from = this.points.length();
                isize k = f.pointsFrom;
                while (k < f.pointsTo) {
                    this.points.add(item: entry.curvePoints()[k]);
                    k = k + 1;
                }
                f.pointsFrom = from;
                f.pointsTo = this.points.length();
            }
            this.filters.add(item: f);
            this.smoothSteps.add(item: Vec3.zero());
            this.smoothShown.add(item: Vec3.zero());
        }
        return fine;
    }

    // One device's entry of a digital action's binding: each control it names, resolved by `@kama/window`'s own names.
    fn void bindEntry(const ref string action, Device device, const ref Optional<ControlEntry> entry, ref BindingError no) {
        string where = deviceName(device: device);
        string whose = "the " + where + " binding of `" + action + "`";
        match (entry) {
            case None: { }
            case Some(value: e): {
                DynamicArray<string> names = DynamicArray.empty();
                Optional<FilterRecord> threshold = Optional::None;
                isize first = this.controls.length();
                if (e.isObject()) {
                    bool fine = true;
                    foreach (string part in e.parts()) {
                        if (part != "control") {
                            no.add(line: whose + " names `" + part + "`, which is no part of a `Digital`'s entry: its controls go under `control`, a name or a list");
                            fine = false;
                        }
                    }
                    foreach (const ref FilterRecord f in e.filters().iterConst()) {
                        if (f.kind != FilterKind::Threshold) {
                            string word = filterWord(kind: f.kind);
                            no.add(line: whose + " lists a `" + word + "`: a `Digital` takes a `threshold` alone of the filters, its press point");
                            fine = false;
                        } else if (device != Device::Gamepad) {
                            no.add(line: whose + " lists a `threshold`: a key or a mouse button is a button already, and a `threshold` makes one from a pad's value");
                            fine = false;
                        } else {
                            match (threshold) {
                                case Some(value: had): {
                                    no.add(line: whose + " lists two thresholds: an entry presses at one point");
                                    fine = false;
                                }
                                case None: {
                                    string why = thresholdRefusal(f: f);
                                    if (why.isEmpty()) { threshold = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                                    else { no.add(line: whose + " " + why); fine = false; }
                                }
                            };
                        }
                    }
                    if (!e.parts().contains(key: "control")) {
                        no.add(line: whose + " names no control: a `Digital`'s entry names its controls under `control`, a name or a list");
                        fine = false;
                    }
                    if (!fine) { return; }
                    foreach (const ref string n in e.parts().getRef(key: "control").iterConst()) { names.add(item: copy n); }
                } else {
                    foreach (const ref string n in e.names().iterConst()) { names.add(item: copy n); }
                }
                foreach (const ref string name in names.iterConst()) {
                    if (device == Device::Gamepad) {
                        this.bindPad(name: name, threshold: threshold, whose: whose, no: no);
                        continue;
                    }
                    Result<int32, Owned<Error>> found = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
                    match (found) {
                        case Ok(value: n): { this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: device, control: n)); }
                        case Err(error: e): {
                            string why = e.message();
                            no.add(line: whose + " names `" + name + "`, which is no " + where + " control: " + why);
                        }
                    };
                }
                DigitalEntry made = DigitalEntry.make(action: cast<int32>(this.entryFirsts.length() - 1));
                made.from = first;
                made.to = this.controls.length();
                made.gestureFrom = this.gestures.length();
                bool kept = this.takeGestures(entry: e, at: this.digitalEntries.length(), device: device, whose: whose, no: no);
                made.gestureTo = this.gestures.length();
                if (kept) { this.digitalEntries.add(item: made); }
            }
        };
    }

    // One pad control of a digital action: a button by its events, or by its travel through `threshold` where the entry
    // has one; a stick's direction by its half, at `threshold` or the `input` record's `stickThreshold`.
    fn void bindPad(const ref string name, const ref Optional<FilterRecord> threshold, const ref string whose, ref BindingError no) {
        string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
        Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
        match (give p) {
            case Ok(value: button): {
                Bound b = Bound.make(device: Device::Gamepad, control: cast<int32>(button));
                match (threshold) {
                    case Some(value: f): {
                        b.kind = SampleKind::Travel;
                        b.press = f.a;
                        b.release = releaseOf(f: f);
                        if (button == PadButton::LeftTrigger || button == PadButton::RightTrigger) { b.zone = Zone::Trigger; }
                    }
                    case None: { }
                };
                this.controls.add(item: b);
                return;
            }
            case Err(error: e): {
                Optional<Source> direction = stickDirection(name: name);
                match (direction) {
                    case Some(value: d): {
                        Optional<FilterRecord> at = match (threshold) { case Some(value: f): threshold; case None: this.stickPress; };
                        match (at) {
                            case Some(value: f): {
                                Bound b = Bound.make(device: Device::Gamepad, control: d.control);
                                b.kind = SampleKind::Axis;
                                b.flip = d.flip;
                                b.half = d.half;
                                b.zone = Zone::Stick;
                                b.press = f.a;
                                b.release = releaseOf(f: f);
                                this.controls.add(item: b);
                            }
                            case None: {
                                no.add(line: whose + " names `" + name + "`, a stick's direction, which as a button needs a press point: the `input` record's `stickThreshold`, or a `threshold` of its own");
                            }
                        };
                    }
                    case None: {
                        string why = e.message();
                        no.add(line: whose + " names `" + name + "`, which is no gamepad control: no button (" + why + ") and no stick's direction (" + directionNames() + ")");
                    }
                };
            }
        };
    }

    // A value action's binding: each device's entry, refused where its kind cannot read it.
    fn void bindValue(ActionKind kind, int32 index, const ref string name, bool delta,
                      const ref SortedMap<string, BindingRecord> bindings, ref BindingError no) {
        if (!bindings.contains(key: name)) { return; }
        borrow bindings.getRef(key: name) as b {
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Keyboard, entry: b.keyboard(), no: no);
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Mouse, entry: b.mouse(), no: no);
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Gamepad, entry: b.gamepad(), no: no);
        }
    }

    // One device's entry of a value action: its shape from its parts, and a source for each control a part names.
    fn void bindValueEntry(ActionKind kind, int32 index, const ref string action, bool delta, Device device,
                           const ref Optional<ControlEntry> entry, ref BindingError no) {
        string where = deviceName(device: device);
        string kindWord = valueKindWord(kind: kind);
        string whose = "the " + where + " binding of `" + action + "`";
        match (entry) {
            case None: { }
            case Some(value: e): {
                foreach (const ref GestureRecord gr in e.gestures().iterConst()) {
                    if (gr.kind != GestureKind::Chord) {
                        string word = gestureWord(kind: gr.kind);
                        no.add(line: whose + " lists a `" + word + "`, which makes a press: only a `Digital` has one, and a `"
                               + kindWord + "` takes a `chord` alone, which gates it while its modifiers are held");
                        return;
                    }
                }
                DynamicArray<string> words = DynamicArray.empty();
                Shape shape = Shape::One;
                if (e.isObject()) {
                    string why = "";
                    shape = shapeOf(kind: kind, entry: e, why: why);
                    if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                        no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                        return;
                    }
                    words = partWords(kind: kind, shape: shape);
                } else if (kind != ActionKind::Analog) {
                    if (kind == ActionKind::Vector2 && device == Device::Mouse && e.names().length() == 1 && e.names()[0] == "Motion") {
                        shape = Shape::Axes2;
                    } else {
                        string parts = kind == ActionKind::Vector2 ? "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, or `x` and `y`, or the mouse's `Motion`"
                                                                   : "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, `forward`, `backward`, or `x`, `y` and `z`";
                        no.add(line: whose + " names a control, and a `" + kindWord + "` is bound by its parts: an object of " + parts);
                        return;
                    }
                }
                Entry made = Entry.make(kind: kind, action: index, shape: shape);
                isize motions = 0;
                isize held = 0;
                isize first = this.sources.length();
                int32 k = 0;
                while (k < 6) {
                    made.firsts[cast<isize>(k)] = this.sources.length();
                    if (cast<isize>(k) < partCount(shape: shape)) {
                        DynamicArray<string> named = namesOf(entry: e, shape: shape, part: k, words: words);
                        foreach (const ref string n in named.iterConst()) {
                            string why = "";
                            Optional<Source> found = valueSourceOf(device: device, name: n, why: why);
                            match (found) {
                                case Some(value: src): {
                                    if (src.kind == SampleKind::Motion) { motions = motions + 1; } else { held = held + 1; }
                                    this.sources.add(item: src);
                                }
                                case None: { no.add(line: whose + " names `" + n + "`, which is no " + where + " control: " + why); }
                            };
                        }
                    }
                    k = k + 1;
                }
                made.firsts[6] = this.sources.length();
                if (motions > 0 && held > 0) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " mixes the mouse's motion, a distance moved, with controls held: bind them in two entries' devices, or to two actions");
                    return;
                }
                if (motions > 0 && !delta) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " names the mouse's motion, a distance moved, so `" + action + "` must be a delta: its record says `\"delta\": true`");
                    return;
                }
                if (motions > 0 && (shape == Shape::Keys2 || shape == Shape::Keys3)) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " names the mouse's motion as a key's part: bind it as `x` and `y`, or as `Motion`");
                    return;
                }
                if (this.sources.length() == first) { return; }
                made.motion = motions > 0;
                made.filterFrom = this.filters.length();
                if (!ownsZone(entry: e)) { this.zoneDefaults(made: made, first: first); }
                bool kept = this.takeFilters(entry: e, motion: made.motion, whose: whose, no: no);
                made.filterTo = this.filters.length();
                if (!kept) { return; }
                made.gateFrom = this.modifiers.length();
                foreach (const ref GestureRecord gr in e.gestures().iterConst()) {
                    string why = "";
                    if (gr.namesTo == gr.namesFrom) { why = "lists a `chord` holding nothing: a chord names a control or an action to hold"; }
                    else { why = this.takeNames(entry: e, r: gr, gesture: -1, device: device); }
                    if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                        no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                        return;
                    }
                }
                made.gateTo = this.modifiers.length();
                isize gated = first;
                while (gated < made.firsts[6]) {
                    this.sources[gated].gate = this.entries.length();
                    gated = gated + 1;
                }
                this.entries.add(item: made);
            }
        };
    }
}

// `t` moved `by` nanoseconds later, held at `NOT_DUE` rather than past it.
fn int64 later(int64 t, int64 by) {
    if (by > 0 && t > NOT_DUE - by) { return NOT_DUE; }
    return t + by;
}

// The share of `of` nanoseconds gone from `from` to `to`, from 0 to 1.
fn float32 shareOf(int64 from, int64 to, int64 of) {
    if (to <= from) { return 0.0; }
    if (of <= 0 || to - from >= of) { return 1.0; }
    float64 gone = cast<float64>(to - from);
    float64 whole = cast<float64>(of);
    return cast<float32>(gone / whole);
}

// The most seconds a gesture's time may be: about 285 years, which the clock's nanoseconds still count.
comptime float64 MOST_SECONDS = 9000000000.0;

// `seconds` in nanoseconds, to the nearest, or -1 where it is out of range: 0 or less (below 0 where `zero` lets it
// be 0), or more than `MOST_SECONDS`.
fn int64 nanosOf(float64 seconds, bool zero) {
    bool fine = seconds > 0.0 || (zero && seconds == 0.0);
    if (!fine || seconds > MOST_SECONDS) { return -1; }
    float64 scaled = seconds * NS_PER_SECOND + 0.5;
    float64 whole = floor(x: scaled);
    return cast<int64>(whole);
}

// A gesture's time in nanoseconds: its own where `own`, else the `input` record's `gestures.<part>`; -1, with `why`
// set, where it has none or it is out of range.
fn int64 nanosFor(bool own, float64 value, Optional<float64> fallback, const ref string word, const ref string part,
                  ref string why) {
    float64 seconds = value;
    if (!own) {
        match (fallback) {
            case Some(value: v): { seconds = v; }
            case None: {
                why = "lists a `" + word + "` naming no time: its own, or the `input` record's `gestures." + part + "`";
                return -1;
            }
        };
    }
    int64 n = nanosOf(seconds: seconds, zero: false);
    if (n < 0) { why = "lists a `" + word + "` of ${seconds} seconds: a gesture's time is more than 0 seconds"; }
    return n;
}

// The `input` record's gesture time `part` refused where it is out of range.
fn void refuseTime(const ref string part, Optional<float64> seconds, ref BindingError no) {
    match (seconds) {
        case Some(value: v): {
            if (nanosOf(seconds: v, zero: false) < 0) {
                no.add(line: "the `input` record's `gestures." + part + "`, ${v} seconds, is no time a gesture waits: it is more than 0 seconds");
            }
        }
        case None: { }
    };
}

fn string gestureWord(GestureKind kind) {
    return match (kind) {
        case Hold: "hold"; case Tap: "tap"; case LongTap: "longTap"; case MultiTap: "multiTap"; case Repeat: "repeat";
        case Toggle: "toggle"; case Delay: "delay"; case Chord: "chord"; case Sequence: "sequence";
        case Interruptible: "interruptible";
    };
}

fn float32 absOf(float32 x) { return x < 0.0 ? -x : x; }
fn float32 signOf(float32 x) { return x > 0.0 ? 1.0 : (x < 0.0 ? -1.0 : 0.0); }

// `x` turned over where `by` is -1; 0 stays 0.
fn float32 invertedBy(float32 x, float32 by) { return by < 0.0 ? 0.0 - x : x; }

// `x`'s size raised to `e`, its sign kept.
fn float32 powered(float32 x, float32 e) {
    if (e == 1.0 || x == 0.0) { return x; }
    float32 a = pow(x: absOf(x: x), y: e);
    return x < 0.0 ? 0.0 - a : a;
}

fn float32 remapped(float32 x, FilterRecord f) { return f.c + (x - f.a) / (f.b - f.a) * (f.d - f.c); }

// `v` on its first `dims` axes, the others 0.
fn Vec3 masked(Vec3 v, int32 dims) {
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x, y: dims >= 2 ? v.y : 0.0, z: dims >= 3 ? v.z : 0.0);
}

fn Vec3 unit(Vec3 v) {
    float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
    if (l2 == 0.0) { return v; }
    float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l, y: v.y / l, z: v.z / l);
}

// A dead zone's one number: 0 inside its lower end; past its upper, 1 scaled or the upper end itself unscaled; between,
// rescaled from 0 to 1 or kept.
fn float32 zoned(float32 size, FilterRecord f) {
    if (size <= f.a) { return 0.0; }
    if (size >= f.b) { return f.scaled ? 1.0 : f.b; }
    return f.scaled ? (size - f.a) / (f.b - f.a) : size;
}

// `v` through a dead zone: on its length, its direction kept, or on each axis apart.
fn Vec3 deadZoned(Vec3 v, FilterRecord f) {
    if (f.radial) {
        float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
        if (l2 == 0.0) { return v; }
        float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
        float32 to = zoned(size: l, f: f);
        return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l * to, y: v.y / l * to, z: v.z / l * to);
    }
    return Vec3.of(x: signOf(x: v.x) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.x), f: f), y: signOf(x: v.y) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.y), f: f),
                   z: signOf(x: v.z) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.z), f: f));
}

// `v` held to a clamp: each axis between its least and its most, or its length to the longest.
fn Vec3 clampedBy(Vec3 v, FilterRecord f) {
    if (f.byLength) {
        float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
        if (l2 <= f.c * f.c) { return v; }
        float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
        return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l * f.c, y: v.y / l * f.c, z: v.z / l * f.c);
    }
    return Vec3.of(x: clampedOne(x: v.x, f: f), y: clampedOne(x: v.y, f: f), z: clampedOne(x: v.z, f: f));
}

fn float32 clampedOne(float32 x, FilterRecord f) {
    float32 low = f.hasA && x < f.a ? f.a : x;
    return f.hasB && low > f.b ? f.b : low;
}

// Whether an entry's own filters name a dead zone, which takes the place of the defaults.
fn bool ownsZone(const ref ControlEntry entry) {
    foreach (const ref FilterRecord f in entry.filters().iterConst()) {
        if (f.kind == FilterKind::DeadZone) { return true; }
    }
    return false;
}

fn string filterWord(FilterKind kind) {
    return match (kind) {
        case DeadZone: "deadZone"; case Scale: "scale"; case Invert: "invert"; case Curve: "curve"; case Clamp: "clamp";
        case Remap: "remap"; case Normalize: "normalize"; case Digital: "digital"; case Smooth: "smooth";
        case Threshold: "threshold";
    };
}

// Why a value entry's filter `f` is refused, or "": a filter the mouse's motion cannot take, a threshold, which makes a
// button, or a number out of its range.
fn string filterRefusal(const ref FilterRecord f, const ref DynamicArray<float32> points, bool motion) {
    string word = filterWord(kind: f.kind);
    bool linear = match (f.kind) { case Scale: true; case Invert: true; case Smooth: true; case _: false; };
    if (motion && !linear) {
        return "puts a `" + word + "` on the mouse's motion, a distance moved, which would change with the step's length: only `scale`, `invert` and `smooth` filter it";
    }
    float32 a = f.a;
    float32 b = f.b;
    match (f.kind) {
        case Threshold: { return "lists a `threshold`: a `threshold` makes a button from a value, so it filters a `Digital`'s entry"; }
        case DeadZone: {
            if (a < 0.0) { return "has a dead zone: its `lower`, ${a}, must be 0 or more"; }
            if (a >= b) { return "has a dead zone: its `lower`, ${a}, must be below its `upper`, ${b}"; }
        }
        case Curve: {
            if (f.points) {
                if (f.pointsTo - f.pointsFrom < 4) { return "has a `curve` of one point: a `curve` through points needs two or more"; }
                isize k = f.pointsFrom + 2;
                while (k < f.pointsTo) {
                    if (points[k] <= points[k - 2]) { return "has a `curve` whose inputs fall or repeat: a `curve`'s points must rise in input"; }
                    k = k + 2;
                }
            } else if (a <= 0.0 || b <= 0.0 || f.c <= 0.0) {
                return "has a `curve` of no rise: a `curve`'s exponent must be more than 0";
            }
        }
        case Clamp: {
            if (!f.hasA && !f.hasB && !f.byLength) { return "has an empty `clamp`: a `clamp` names its `min`, its `max` or its `length`"; }
            if (f.hasA && f.hasB && a > b) { return "has a `clamp` past itself: a `clamp`'s `min` must be at most its `max`"; }
            if (f.byLength && f.c <= 0.0) { return "has a `clamp` of no length: a `clamp`'s `length` must be more than 0"; }
        }
        case Remap: {
            if (a == b) { return "has a `remap` from one number: a `remap`'s `from` must span a range"; }
        }
        case Smooth: {
            if (a <= 0.0) { return "has a `smooth` of no time: a `smooth`'s seconds must be more than 0"; }
        }
        case _: { }
    };
    return "";
}
fn float32 lengthSquared(Vec3 v) { return v.x * v.x + v.y * v.y + v.z * v.z; }

// A direction no longer than 1: keys pressed together, a diagonal.
fn Vec3 clamped(Vec3 v) {
    float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
    if (l2 <= 1.0) { return v; }
    float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l, y: v.y / l, z: v.z / l);
}

// A stick's direction by kyoten's own name: its axis, turned over for a Y so up is positive, and its half.
fn Optional<Source> stickDirection(const ref string name) {
    int32 axis = -1;
    float32 half = 0.0;
    if (name == "LeftStickUp") { axis = 1; half = 1.0; }
    else if (name == "LeftStickDown") { axis = 1; half = -1.0; }
    else if (name == "LeftStickLeft") { axis = 0; half = -1.0; }
    else if (name == "LeftStickRight") { axis = 0; half = 1.0; }
    else if (name == "RightStickUp") { axis = 3; half = 1.0; }
    else if (name == "RightStickDown") { axis = 3; half = -1.0; }
    else if (name == "RightStickLeft") { axis = 2; half = -1.0; }
    else if (name == "RightStickRight") { axis = 2; half = 1.0; }
    if (axis < 0) { return Optional::None; }
    Source s = Source.make(device: Device::Gamepad, kind: SampleKind::Axis, control: axis, flip: axis == 1 || axis == 3);
    s.half = half;
    return Optional::Some(value: s);
}

fn string directionNames() {
    return "`LeftStickUp`, `LeftStickDown`, `LeftStickLeft`, `LeftStickRight`, `RightStickUp`, `RightStickDown`, `RightStickLeft` or `RightStickRight`";
}

// Where a threshold lets go: its own `release`, else three quarters of its press.
fn float32 releaseOf(FilterRecord f) { return f.hasB ? f.b : f.a * 0.75; }

// Why a threshold is refused, or "": a press point from above 0 to 1, a release point from 0 to below it.
fn string thresholdRefusal(FilterRecord f) {
    float32 press = f.a;
    float32 release = releaseOf(f: f);
    if (press <= 0.0 || press > 1.0) { return "has a `threshold` pressing at ${press}: a `threshold`'s `press` is above 0 and at most 1"; }
    if (release < 0.0 || release >= press) {
        return "has a `threshold` letting go at ${release}: a `threshold`'s `release` is from 0 to below its `press`, ${press}";
    }
    return "";
}

// The kind of the action named `name`, as a records file writes it, or "" when the game declares none of that name.
fn string kindOf(const ref ActionList actions, const ref string name) {
    if (actions.digitalNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Digital"; }
    if (actions.analogNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Analog"; }
    if (actions.vector2Names().contains(item: name)) { return "Vector2"; }
    if (actions.vector3Names().contains(item: name)) { return "Vector3"; }
    if (actions.poseNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Pose"; }
    return "";
}

fn string valueKindWord(ActionKind kind) {
    return match (kind) { case Analog: "Analog"; case Vector2: "Vector2"; case Vector3: "Vector3"; case _: "value"; };
}

fn string deviceName(Device device) {
    return match (device) { case Keyboard: "keyboard"; case Mouse: "mouse"; case Gamepad: "gamepad"; };
}

// How many parts a shape reads.
fn isize partCount(Shape shape) {
    return match (shape) { case One: 1; case Pair: 2; case Keys2: 4; case Axes2: 2; case Keys3: 6; case Axes3: 3; };
}

// The words of a shape's parts, in their order.
fn DynamicArray<string> partWords(ActionKind kind, Shape shape) {
    DynamicArray<string> w = DynamicArray.empty();
    match (shape) {
        case One: { }
        case Pair: { w.add(item: "positive"); w.add(item: "negative"); }
        case Keys2: { w.add(item: "up"); w.add(item: "down"); w.add(item: "left"); w.add(item: "right"); }
        case Axes2: { w.add(item: "x"); w.add(item: "y"); }
        case Keys3: {
            w.add(item: "up"); w.add(item: "down"); w.add(item: "left"); w.add(item: "right"); w.add(item: "forward");
            w.add(item: "backward");
        }
        case Axes3: { w.add(item: "x"); w.add(item: "y"); w.add(item: "z"); }
    };
    return w;
}

// The shape an object entry's words make for `kind`, or why they make none (`why` set).
fn Shape shapeOf(ActionKind kind, const ref ControlEntry entry, ref string why) {
    bool keys = false;
    bool axes = false;
    bool pair = false;
    string unknown = "";
    foreach (string w in entry.parts()) {
        if (w == "positive" || w == "negative") { pair = true; }
        else if (w == "up" || w == "down" || w == "left" || w == "right" || w == "forward" || w == "backward") { keys = true; }
        else if (w == "x" || w == "y" || w == "z") { axes = true; }
        else if (unknown.isEmpty()) { unknown = copy w; }
        if ((w == "forward" || w == "backward" || w == "z") && kind != ActionKind::Vector3 && unknown.isEmpty()) { unknown = copy w; }
    }
    string allowed = match (kind) {
        case Analog: "`positive` and `negative`";
        case Vector2: "`up`, `down`, `left` and `right`, or `x` and `y`";
        case Vector3: "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, `forward` and `backward`, or `x`, `y` and `z`";
        case _: "none";
    };
    string kindWord = valueKindWord(kind: kind);
    if (!unknown.isEmpty() || (kind == ActionKind::Analog && (keys || axes)) || (kind != ActionKind::Analog && pair)) {
        string named = unknown.isEmpty() ? "a part" : "`" + unknown + "`";
        why = "names " + named + ", which is no part of a `" + kindWord + "`: its parts are " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (keys && axes) {
        why = "names both keys' parts and axes: a `" + kindWord + "`'s entry is one or the other, " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (!keys && !axes && !pair) {
        why = "is an object naming no part: a `" + kindWord + "`'s parts are " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (pair) { return Shape::Pair; }
    if (kind == ActionKind::Vector2) { return keys ? Shape::Keys2 : Shape::Axes2; }
    return keys ? Shape::Keys3 : Shape::Axes3;
}

// The names a part of an entry reads: an entry written as a name or a list reads them all as its one part; the mouse's
// `Motion` reads its two axes; an object's part reads what its word names, none when it names none.
fn DynamicArray<string> namesOf(const ref ControlEntry entry, Shape shape, int32 part, const ref DynamicArray<string> words) {
    DynamicArray<string> named = DynamicArray.empty();
    if (!entry.isObject()) {
        if (shape == Shape::Axes2) {
            named.add(item: part == 0 ? "MotionX" : "MotionY");
            return named;
        }
        foreach (const ref string n in entry.names().iterConst()) { named.add(item: copy n); }
        return named;
    }
    string word = copy words[cast<isize>(part)];
    if (!entry.parts().contains(key: word)) { return named; }
    foreach (const ref string n in entry.parts().getRef(key: word).iterConst()) { named.add(item: copy n); }
    return named;
}

// A digital control's number from its name, read by `@kama/window`'s own reader for its device: a `Key`'s USB HID usage
// id, a `PointerButton`'s W3C button, a `PadButton`'s W3C standard index. The reader's refusal lists every name.
fn Result<int32, Owned<Error>> controlOf(Device device, const ref string name) {
    string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
    match (device) {
        case Keyboard: {
            Result<Key, Owned<Error>> k = deserializeJsonBuffer::<Key>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give k) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
        case Mouse: {
            Result<PointerButton, Owned<Error>> b = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PointerButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give b) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
        case Gamepad: {
            Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give p) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
    };
}


// A value's control from its name, or none with `why` set: a key, a mouse button or a pad button's edge or travel by
// `@kama/window`'s readers, a pad's stick axis by `PadAxis` (its Y turned over), or the mouse's `MotionX` or `MotionY`
// (its Y turned over). A reader's refusal lists every name.
fn Optional<Source> valueSourceOf(Device device, const ref string name, ref string why) {
    string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
    match (device) {
        case Keyboard: {
            Result<int32, Owned<Error>> k = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
            match (give k) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Control, control: v, flip: false)); }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    why = e.message();
                    return Optional::None;
                }
            };
        }
        case Mouse: {
            if (name == "MotionX") { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Motion, control: 0, flip: false)); }
            if (name == "MotionY") { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Motion, control: 1, flip: true)); }
            Result<int32, Owned<Error>> b = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
            match (give b) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Control, control: v, flip: false)); }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    string asButton = e.message();
                    why = asButton + "; nor the mouse's motion, `MotionX` or `MotionY`";
                    return Optional::None;
                }
            };
        }
        case Gamepad: {
            Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give p) {
                case Ok(value: v): {
                    return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Travel, control: cast<int32>(v), flip: false));
                }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    string asButton = e.message();
                    Result<PadAxis, Owned<Error>> x = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadAxis>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
                    match (give x) {
                        case Ok(value: axis): {
                            bool turned = axis == PadAxis::LeftY || axis == PadAxis::RightY;
                            return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Axis, control: cast<int32>(axis), flip: turned));
                        }
                        case Err(error: f): {
                            Optional<Source> direction = stickDirection(name: name);
                            match (direction) {
                                case Some(value: d): { return direction; }
                                case None: { }
                            };
                            string asAxis = f.message();
                            why = "no button (" + asButton + ") and no stick's axis (" + asAxis + "), nor a stick's direction (" + directionNames() + ")";
                            return Optional::None;
                        }
                    };
                }
            };
        }
    };
}
